{
  "id": "ep234",
  "duration": 47.769,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.551,
      "text": "A Soviet probe survived hell and whispered secrets from another world.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Art By Don Davis Artist's concept of one of the probes on the hot surface of Venus (ARC-1977-AC77-0475-9).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Ames Research Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Art_By_Don_Davis_Artist%27s_concept_of_one_of_the_probes_on_the_hot_surface_of_Venus_(ARC-1977-AC77-0475-9).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.633,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 1.633,
          "end": 4.567,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.551,
      "end": 11.521,
      "text": "In August 1970, Venera 7 launched to conquer the most hostile environment in the solar system.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.567,
          "end": 11.533,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.521,
      "end": 18.366,
      "text": "Engineers built its heavy titanium hull to withstand 180 atmospheres of crushing pressure.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Cut-away model of a Soviet Venera 12 lander.jpg",
        "credit": "Don S. Montgomery, U.S. Navy (Ret.)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cut-away_model_of_a_Soviet_Venera_12_lander.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.533,
          "end": 18.367,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.366,
      "end": 24.086,
      "text": "During descent, the parachute failed and plunged the robotic lander into a severe freefall.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "1972 CPA 4166.jpg",
        "credit": "USSR Post",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1972_CPA_4166.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.367,
          "end": 24.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.086,
      "end": 31.086,
      "text": "It slammed into the dark side of Venus on December 15, 1970, and abruptly went silent.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA23791-Venus-RealAndEnhancedContrastViews-20200608 (cropped).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA23791-Venus-RealAndEnhancedContrastViews-20200608_(cropped).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.1,
          "end": 31.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 31.086,
      "end": 36.581,
      "text": "Weeks later, astronomers found a faint signal buried deep within the background noise.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "\u0420\u0422-70.jpg",
        "credit": "90Van",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A0%D0%A2-70.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 31.1,
          "end": 36.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.581,
      "end": 42.831,
      "text": "Landing on its side pointed the antenna away, hiding twenty-three precious minutes of history.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Venera 9 Space Probe 01.jpg",
        "credit": "Stolbovsky",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venera_9_Space_Probe_01.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.567,
          "end": 39.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 39.7,
          "end": 42.833,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.831,
      "end": 47.419,
      "text": "That incredible hidden transmission proved our Soviet probe survived hell.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Art By Don Davis Artist's concept of one of the probes on the hot surface of Venus (ARC-1977-AC77-0475-9).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Ames Research Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Art_By_Don_Davis_Artist%27s_concept_of_one_of_the_probes_on_the_hot_surface_of_Venus_(ARC-1977-AC77-0475-9).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 42.833,
          "end": 47.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
